{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>I will surely return to you.</b> Two returns: one in Tishrei and one in Nisan. <b>At the living season</b> — the angels know that they live forever; therefore they said <b>at the living season</b>, meaning: next year, at this same season when we are alive and enduring, I will return to you. But Elisha son of Yoram was destined for death; he did not know whether he would live until the next year, therefore he did not say 'I will surely return' but only 'at the living season.'" "<b>כעת חיה.</b> Rashi explained: since it is not read כְּעֵת חָיָה — meaning, the kaf of כעת is not pointed with a shva, for if it were with a shva, it would mean 'like a living thing of the field.'" "<b>והוא אחריו.</b> Targum Yonatan translates: 'and Yishmael was standing behind me.' Meaning, behind the angel, so that Sarah would not interact with the angels, for she thought they were human beings."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {2 "Chizkuni quotes Rashi's grammatical note distinguishing כָּעֵת (with qamatz, 'at the time') from כְּעֵת (with shva, 'like a living creature'). I rendered the unpointed Hebrew forms as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:40.940500783Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}